# Everything here is either useless in the image or expensive to send to the
# daemon. .venv alone was 165 MB of a 170 MB context, and __pycache__ is worse
# than useless: `COPY src .` carried the host's .pyc files (including ones built
# for a Python the image does not have), and rewriting them locally invalidated
# that layer and every layer after it.
#
# The `**/` on the cache patterns is load-bearing: Docker matches a bare
# `__pycache__/` against the context root only, so it missed src/__pycache__ and
# 55 .pyc files still reached the image.
.git/
.github/
.githooks/
.claude/
.idea/
.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
docs/
html_samples/
CHANGELOG.md
CLAUDE.md
CLAUDE.local.md.example
Handoff.md
README.md
